# The Now Playing visualizer's PCM tap (apps/ipodui/viz_tap.c,
# docs/research/bcm2722/visualizer.md section 11): while a song plays the
# tap delivers fresh, unsilent windows of 512 samples; a book (the mini
# library's M4B) is refused, by the audiobook Now Playing's own flag; and
# after a stop the tap gives no fresh window (the mixer's 3 s of padding
# reads as silence, then the head stops: stale). No shell screen uses the tap yet,
# so the script drives it from the script thread.
#   SIM_BUILD=build/sim-ui scripts/shots.sh tests/ui/ipodui-p19-viztap.script
# golden: skip
# fulls-extra: 2   (the main menu gains its Now Playing row at the first play_files and loses it at audio_stop)
# log: viz_tap ok (sound)
# log: viz_tap ok (book)
# log: viz_tap ok (quiet)
# nolog: viz_tap failed

wait 3000
play_files /Music/Tone%20Collective/Sine%20Studies/01%20Concert%20A.mp3
wait 2500
expect_playing 300
viz_tap 2000 512 sound
viz_tap 1000 256 sound
shot playing
play_files /Music/Fixture%20Author/Mini%20Audiobook/Mini%20Audiobook.m4b
wait 2500
expect_playing 300
viz_tap 1000 512 book
audio_stop
wait 500
viz_tap 500 512 quiet
